# 🧠 General Rules

- Always use TypeScript
- Prefer functional components in React
- Use TailwindCSS for styling
- Use **`tailwind-variants`** (`import { tv } from 'tailwind-variants'`) when the component has real variant axes (color, size, variant, placement, etc.); use **`cn`** from **`src/utils/cn`** for layout-only class composition and Tailwind conflict merging (re-exports `cn` from `tailwind-variants`, backed by `tailwind-merge`). See **`docs/styling-utilities.md`**
- Avoid inline styles
- Prefer composition over complex logic
- Keep components small, reusable and isolated

---

# 📁 Project Structure

### .storybook

- Contains all Storybook configuration
- Includes addons, themes and preview setup
- Do NOT add component logic here

---

### documentation

- Contains layouts used in Storybook Docs
- Responsible for documentation structure
- Must be reusable
- Do NOT include business logic

---

### src/components

- Contains all Design System components
- Each component MUST follow the structure defined in:

docs/component-structure.md

IMPORTANT:

- Do not create components outside this pattern
- Always include stories
- Keep consistency across components

---

### src/styles/global.css

- Global TailwindCSS configuration
- Responsible for:
  - resets
  - design tokens
  - base styles

Avoid:

- component-specific styles
- unnecessary overrides

---

# 🧩 Module Structure (Components)

Each component must follow:
ComponentName/
├── ComponentName.tsx
├── stories/
│ ├── configs/
│ │ ├── argTypes.ts
│ │ └── docs-pages.tsx
│ ├── general.story.tsx
│ ├── with-background.story.tsx
│ └── with-border.story.tsx

Rules:

- Keep component logic minimal
- Stories are mandatory
- Use configs for reuse
- Prefer args over hardcoded values

---

# 🎯 Component Rules

- Must be reusable and composable
- Avoid tight coupling
- Extract logic into hooks or utils
- Use clear naming
- Props must be typed

---

# 🧪 Storybook Rules

- Every component must have stories
- **One story file per meaningful variation** (e.g. color, size, variant, disabled/read-only): use dedicated `*.story.tsx` files so each axis is visible in the sidebar—not only toggles on `general`
- Use argTypes for controls
- Use docs-pages.tsx for layout
- Avoid duplication (share args via `stories/configs/`)
- Represent real use cases

---
